{"id":"2ef90c1cbce2936f","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-simple-ring.md","title":"Simple Ring","display":"df-simple-ring — Simple Ring","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-simple-ring","aliases":["58-df-simple-ring","Simple Ring"],"display":"df-simple-ring — Simple Ring","depends_on":["[[58-df-ring]]","[[58-df-artinian]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-simple-ring"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-simple-ring</span><span>Simple Ring</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-simple-ring — Simple Ring"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"58-df-ring\">58-df-ring</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0ad886c6bc35a838\" href=\"?note=0ad886c6bc35a838\" title=\"58-df-artinian\">58-df-artinian</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\">\\((R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\)</span> (unital ring)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\subseteq R\">\\(I\\subseteq R\\)</span> (two-sided-ideal candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ring}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\)</span> (ring predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"58-df-ring\">58-df-ring</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\">\\(\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\)</span> (left-Artinian predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0ad886c6bc35a838\" href=\"?note=0ad886c6bc35a838\" title=\"58-df-artinian\">58-df-artinian</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S\\)</span> (simple-ring predicate defined in this file)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S\\)</span> (simple-Artinian predicate defined in this file)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land0_R\\ne1_R\\land\\forall I\\subseteq R\\;\\Bigl(\\bigl(0_R\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x-y\\in I)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(r\\cdot x\\in I\\land x\\cdot r\\in I)\\bigr)\\to(I=\\{0_R\\}\\lor I=R)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land0_R\\ne1_R\\land\\forall I\\subseteq R\\;\\Bigl(\\bigl(0_R\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x-y\\in I)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(r\\cdot x\\in I\\land x\\cdot r\\in I)\\bigr)\\to(I=\\{0_R\\}\\lor I=R)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring\\text{-}carrier} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R)\\leftrightarrow\\exists+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R\\in V\\;\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring\\text{-}carrier} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R)\\leftrightarrow\\exists+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R\\in V\\;\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}artinian\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}artinian\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom uses the nonzero unital convention for simple rings.</li>\n<li>Artin-Wedderburn: every simple Artinian ring is isomorphic to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M_n(D)\">\\(M_n(D)\\)</span> for some division ring <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D\">\\(D\\)</span></li>\n<li>A zero Jacobson radical implies semiprimitivity; the matrix-product structure theorem additionally requires an Artinian hypothesis.</li>\n<li>Kernels of ring homomorphisms are two-sided ideals.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Herstein, Noncommutative Rings</li>\n<li>Lam, A First Course in Noncommutative Rings</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-ring","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ring]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-artinian","status":"resolved","id":"0ad886c6bc35a838","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-artinian]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ring","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Ring}_S$ (ring predicate, see [[58-df-ring]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-artinian","status":"resolved","id":"0ad886c6bc35a838","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)$ (left-Artinian predicate, see [[58-df-artinian]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)","display":false},{"tex":"I\\subseteq R","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ring}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land0_R\\ne1_R\\land\\forall I\\subseteq R\\;\\Bigl(\\bigl(0_R\\in I\\land\\forall x,y\\in I\\;(x-y\\in I)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in I\\;(r\\cdot x\\in I\\land x\\cdot r\\in I)\\bigr)\\to(I=\\{0_R\\}\\lor I=R)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}ring\\text{-}carrier} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R)\\leftrightarrow\\exists+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R\\in V\\;\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}simple\\text{-}artinian\\text{-}ring} \\vdash \\operatorname{SimpleArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{SimpleRing}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)\\land\\mathrm{LeftArtinian}_S(R,+,\\cdot,0_R,1_R)","display":true},{"tex":"M_n(D)","display":false},{"tex":"D","display":false}],"bytes":1952,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1171","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-simple-ring.md|58-df-simple-ring]]（batch16）"}],"o